// The type check of CI (RV-I05, docs/ci.md section 5): basedpyright over the compiler and the checker, in pyright's
// standard mode, in the locked virtualenv. scripts/lint.sh runs it; it fails only on an error that
// .basedpyright/baseline.json does not hold.
// `canon` is on the path: its editable install is an import hook that basedpyright does not follow (D08).
{
  "include": ["compiler/rezono_compiler", "checker/rezono_checker"],
  "typeCheckingMode": "standard",
  "pythonVersion": "3.13",
  "pythonPlatform": "Linux",
  "extraPaths": ["canon"]
}
